# Sentinel — copy to `.env` beside your compose file. Every line here is OPTIONAL: the stack comes up
# with none of them set. They exist because a few defaults cannot be guessed correctly for everybody.
#
#   cp .env.example .env      # then edit
#
# `docker compose` reads `.env` from the directory it runs in, automatically. Nothing else does — the
# air-gapped bundle's own `.env` (OLLAMA_IMAGE_TAG) is generated by build-airgap-bundle.sh and is a
# different file with a different purpose.

# --- WHO THE CONTAINERS RUN AS (HEALTH-005 PR-C) --------------------------------------------------
#
# ⚠ THE ONE TRAP IN THIS FILE. `UID` and `GID` are SHELL variables, not environment variables: your
# shell sets `UID` for itself and does NOT export it, so `${UID:-1000}` in the compose file reads an
# EMPTY environment and silently falls back to 1000 — for everybody, including you.
#
# That is fine on a host where you are uid 1000, which is the common case and why it is the default.
# It is wrong, silently, anywhere else: the containers would write files owned by a uid that is not
# yours, and you would be back to needing sudo to clean up ./runs and ./state.
#
# Two ways to make it true. Either uncomment and fill these in with YOUR numbers (`id -u`, `id -g`):
#
#UID=1000
#GID=1000
#
# or export them in the shell that runs compose, which keeps this file free of machine-specific values:
#
#   export UID GID && docker compose up
#
# Why it matters at all: the image declares no USER, so without this the containers run as root and
# everything they create under ./runs and ./state is root-owned on the host — uncleanable without
# sudo (renaming a directory writes to the directory itself, so owning the parent does not help),
# breaking `go test ./...` on a checkout, and making the service journal unreadable from the host.
#
# ⚠ MIGRATION, if your stack has run before: files created by the earlier root-running containers are
# still root-owned, and the store-gateway will not be able to open its own database under the new
# user. One command, once:
#
#   sudo chown -R "$(id -u):$(id -g)" ./runs ./state ./config

# --- MODEL / RUNTIME ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Absent key -> the deterministic heuristic planner and L1-L6 heal. Still a working product offline.
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# A local OpenAI-compatible endpoint (the `ollama` profile, or one you already run elsewhere).
# See docs/LOCAL_MODELS.md for the model catalogue.
#LLM_BACKEND=openai
#LLM_BASE_URL=http://ollama:11434/v1
#LLM_MODEL=qwen3:8b
#LLM_API_KEY=noauth

# --- CONTROL-API ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unset, control-api generates a token and persists it to ./state/control-api.token (0600), reusing
# it across restarts. Set it to manage the value yourself; CONTROL_API_AUTOTOKEN=0 for a read-only
# instance with no token at all.
#CONTROL_API_TOKEN=

# Mode 3 (recommended): control-api serves the browser UI from its own port, same-origin, so the CORS
# allowlist can be emptied. See the walkthrough at the top of docker-compose.yml.
#CONTROL_API_SERVE_UI=1
#CONTROL_API_CORS_ORIGINS=

# --- RELEASE PINNING (docker-compose.ghcr.yml only) -----------------------------------------------
# Unset means :latest, which a pre-release never claims. Pin a tag to be explicit.
#SENTINEL_VERSION=v0.1.0
